{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1466987-exalts-and-excellencies-playing-exalted-with-mutants-and-masterminds-3e-rules","id":1466987,"title":"\"Exalts and Excellencies\"-- Playing Exalted with Mutants and Masterminds 3e Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-06T13:52:28-07:00","id":1466987,"title":"\"Exalts and Excellencies\"-- Playing Exalted with Mutants and Masterminds 3e Rules","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Exalted has an awesome setting of fantasy superheroes, but complicated mechanics that break down if pressed too far. Mutants and Masterminds has excellent mechanics for playing superheroes, but is oriented towards modern adventures. I tried to unite the two </span></span><a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?258324-Exalts-and-Excellencies-playing-Exalted-using-Mutants-and-Masterminds-rules&amp;p=14044941\" target=\"_blank\">a long time ago</a><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">, but it it didn't work particularly well. But I've learned a lot more about game design since then, and a new and superior edition of Exalted has been released and grown into a fairly mature game. So... time to try again, perhaps.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">I think my previous attempt ran into trouble because I was trying not to depart too far from the basic M&amp;M rules</span></span><sup>1</sup><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">-- but at the same time, I was trying to import mote expenditure/anima rules with much more granularity than the system allowed. I'm not going to do that again. I'm keeping the core M&amp;M rules for powers and action, but I'm taking a hatchet to the superficial structure of the game. If nothing else, I intend to replace the lingering D&amp;D trappings with equally-insubstantial Exalted ones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><img src=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/images/smilies/smallstick/smalltongue.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">But anyway.</span></span><br /> <hr /> <i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Unless otherwise specified, all rules from the Hero's Handbook still apply normally.</span></span></i><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><i><u>Core System</u></i></b></span></span></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><b><u>Ranks and Measures</u></b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Superhero capabilities scale faster and reach greater heights than even Celestial Exalts. Use the following Ranks and Measures table in place of the one presented in the Hero's Handbook. Because the values don't increase at the same consistent rates, you cannot calculate speed simply by adding Time and Distance ranks--you have to actually do the math. Or look at the &quot;SPEED&quot; column, where the numbers are already worked out and rounded off nicely for you.</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Note that the alternate table isn't required for the rest of the rules to work. This is my interpretation of what sort of benchmarks fit with the lore and mechanics of Exalted. If you have a more generous view of what Solars can do, feel free to use the original Ranks and Measures table.</i><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table_cms_table_grid text